<pending_commit branch="chromeos-2016.05" change_id="Ibe7bfc94b3e3d11ba881399a39f9915991c89d8c" commit="f5f995eed008180bda0a2984ef73243b6332d025" commit_message="UPSTREAM: elog: Ensure eventlog will always get initialized when configured in  Commit 0d9cd92e (chromeos: Clean up elog handling) removed the individual elog_init() calls from mainboards that did them and automated adding certain events through the boot state machine. Unfortunately, the new code would sometimes not log any specific event at all, and thereby also never call elog_init() (through elog_add_event()) which adds the &quot;System boot&quot; event.  We can assume that any board that configures the eventlog at all actually wants to use it, so let's just add another call to elog_init() to the boot state machine so we can ensure it gets called at least once.  BRANCH=None BUG=chrome-os-partner:56001 TEST=Booted Kevin, confirmed that eventlog code runs again.  Signed-off-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://review.coreboot.org/16118 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Change-Id: Ibe7bfc94b3e3d11ba881399a39f9915991c89d8c Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/368946 Commit-Ready: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="368946" owner_email="furquan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/46/368946/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2016.05" change_id="Id89a526106d1989c2bd3416ab81913e6cf743d17" commit="0f9ffb40e2dc78c2efb5815c43599b381e1ad53a" commit_message="UPSTREAM: soc/apollolake: add GPIO SMI support  GPIOs which trigger SMIs set the GPIO_SMI_STS status bits in SMI_STS register. This patch also sets the SMI_EN bit in enable register for each community based on GPIOROUTSMI bit in gpio pad. When SMI on a gpio happens status needs to be gathered on gpio number which is done by reading the GPI_SMI_STS and GPI_SMI_EN registers.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:54977 BRANCH=None  TEST=When system is in firmware mode executing the command      lidclose from ec console shuts down the system.  Signed-off-by: Shaunak Saha &lt;shaunak.saha@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://review.coreboot.org/15833 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Change-Id: Id89a526106d1989c2bd3416ab81913e6cf743d17 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/368947 Commit-Ready: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="368947" owner_email="furquan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/47/368947/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2016.05" change_id="I8ff6001e48dcbbd4cee5097e759352d8fea6189b" commit="ee742a9e670b1c0d2c5589ae87b44e99a579ded8" commit_message="UPSTREAM: google/reef: Add mainboard handler function for gpio SMI  This patch adds mainboard_smi_gpi_handler which handles the SMI event. This can happen in situations like lidclose and system goes to shutdown.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:54977 BRANCH=None  TEST=When system is in firmware mode executing the command      lidclose from ec console shuts down the system.  Signed-off-by: Shaunak Saha &lt;shaunak.saha@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://review.coreboot.org/15834 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Change-Id: I8ff6001e48dcbbd4cee5097e759352d8fea6189b Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/368948 Commit-Ready: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="368948" owner_email="furquan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/48/368948/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2016.05" change_id="Idbc58179c7b45160afef7d7e44f9b3b334f8c4a7" commit="96874eba34dc7c7505a41843a61e72092ab1ae16" commit_message="UPSTREAM: Makefile.inc: Strip CONFIG_DEVICETREE quotes at top of makefile  Minor change - Instead of stripping the quotes from CONFIG_DEVICETREE inline, add it to the location where we normalize all the other Kconfig variables.  BUG=None BRANCH=None TEST=None  Signed-off-by: Martin Roth &lt;martinroth@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://review.coreboot.org/16116 Reviewed-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@google.com&gt; Change-Id: Idbc58179c7b45160afef7d7e44f9b3b334f8c4a7 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/368949 Commit-Ready: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="368949" owner_email="furquan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/49/368949/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2016.05" change_id="Ib434ce92bdbc49180fb3f713b26d65ba4cf8c441" commit="e01e63a35cb51f9c3bbd9c8b6622bee27e16c08b" commit_message="UPSTREAM: Makefiles: Use $(MAINBOARD_DIR) instead of $(CONFIG_MAINBOARD_DIR)  The variable MAINBOARD_DIR already has the quotes stripped off.  BUG=None BRANCH=None TEST=None  Signed-off-by: Martin Roth &lt;martinroth@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://review.coreboot.org/16117  Reviewed-by: Lee Leahy &lt;leroy.p.leahy@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@google.com&gt; Change-Id: Ib434ce92bdbc49180fb3f713b26d65ba4c